         <change when="2026-06-19T14:58:09-04:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/ngonis">Finalized - done</change>
         <change when="2026-06-19T14:33:20-04:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/ngonis">Vote - Accept-Straight-to-Finalization - Following discussion with CB, the corrections will become  &lt;:με̣τ̣έ̣χ̣[ε]ιν̣ &lt;:[πυ]ν4.- θάνομαι|reg|[πυ]ν̣4.- θάνομε̣:&gt;=PN C. Balamoshev (from image and parallels)|ed|με̣.8 &lt;:αἰσθάνομαι|reg|α̣ἰ̣[σ]4.- θάνομε̣:&gt;:&gt;. The rest of the text will checked before finalization.</change>
         <change when="2025-01-05T18:33:11-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/costasbala">Submit - Correction of a typo in line 3, and revision of the verb.</change>
         <change when="2025-01-05T18:32:35-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/costasbala">Commit - I've corrected a typo in lines 3-4 as the edition had α̣ἰ̣[σ]|θάνομε (l. αἰσθάνομαι) and not αἰσ|θάνομε̣ (l. α̣ἰ[σ]|θάνομαι). However, I read [πυ]ν̣|θάνομε̣ (l. πυνθάνομαι) here, a prefectural "cliché", also encountered in SB 18.13715.11, SB 20.14662.3, P.Lips. 2.145v.2. Rea had also conjectured other plausible readings, some of which can be probably verified, at least for the εὐθέως after δεσπότες in line 8, where ε̣ὐθ̣ can be read. </change>
